# charon integration step 36 after 546078ea5d: commit ac60733caed8178411071c5b4ed88994a657ea7f
# first parent 5bb203828ea85c38ca598124abaabb68d5cec4b1
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: canonical name patterns and prefix-indexed pattern matching
#
# Name patterns can now spell out every item name: `name#N` selects the path element with
# disambiguator N (closures, `_` items, macro-generated duplicates), the unnamed elements
# `{vtable}`, `{const}`, ... are identifiers, `@` is a type parameter (so `{impl T for Pair<@>}`
# differs from `{impl T for Pair<u8>}`), and literal types (`u8`) and tuples (`Tuple<A, B>`, with
# `Tuple` the unit type) match. `Pattern::canonical_with` renders the most precise pattern for a
# name, with `#0` where a sibling has the same identifier (`Disambiguation`).
#
# `PatternIndex` stores patterns in a trie keyed by path identifiers (impl blocks share one key), so
# matching a name against thousands of `--opaque`/`--include`/`--exclude` or start-from patterns
# costs O(name length) plus the candidates, with the same most-precise-wins result. Start-from
# pattern lists split at commas outside brackets. reorder_decls exposes `item_dependencies`, the
# per-item edges of the declaration graph.

